"May be on your ballot: only voters in this district vote on this seat. Check your official sample ballot at IndianaVoters.in.gov.","maybe":true,"ballotOrder":420,"candidates":[{"name":"Adam S Lehman","party":"republican","status":"candidate"},{"name":"Mitch Sprunger","party":null,"status":"candidate"}]}],"referendums":[{"id":"in-adams-q-public-question-1","name":"Public Question #1","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Currently, under the Constitution of the State of Indiana, a person charged with murder or treason is not entitled to be released on bail if the proof is evident or the presumption strong. Shall the Constitution of the State of Indiana be amended to provide that a person charged with an offense other than murder or treason is not entitled to bail if:\n(1) the proof is evident or the presumption strong; and\n(2) the state proves by clear and convincing evidence that no release conditions will reasonably protect the safety of any other person or the community.\n(This question concerns Article 1, Section 17 of the Constitution of the State of Indiana.)"},{"id":"in-adams-q-public-question-2","name":"Public Question #2","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the Constitution of the State of Indiana be amended to permit the judge of a city or town court to reside in: (1) the county in which the court is located; or (2) the bordering county closest to the city or town in which the court is located? (This question concerns Article 6, Section 6 of the Constitution of the State of Indiana.)"},{"id":"in-adams-q-court-of-appeals-judicial-retention-fourth-district","name":"Court of Appeals Judicial Retention - Fourth District","type":"Court Of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Judge Mary A. DeBoer be retained in office?"},{"id":"in-adams-q-court-of-appeals-judicial-retention-fifth-district","name":"Court of Appeals Judic